Thanks for downloading this.This game is pretty simple to understand, basically the objective is to put the ball in the other player's "basket" (the red things moving on the edges of the screen). To do that, you have to catch the ball with your ship and release it so that the ballistic trajectory of the ball ends in the basket. You can shoot green things (don't ask) that when hitting the enemy, will force him to release the ball. There are also green "force barriers" whose sole purpose is to limit how close you can get to your enemy's basket. They will kick you back if you touch them, which is not necessarily a bad thing.The game has a pretty complete physics model, actually its what I'm proud of. Every object is treated as a body, the ships generate forces with their engines (measured in Newtons) and they have their own mass, which determines the acceleration they recieve. Why do they tilt when moving? Don't ask. I just thought it looked cool. There is also an atmosphere in the game that offers resistance to advance. The faster you go, the more difficult is for you to go faster. (yeah, I know the background is space, but what the heck). You may notice that when you are holding the ball you are more sluggish. That is because you become heavier and offer more resistance to advance when holding an object. This game is a two player game, because I think its funnier that way (and I didn't want to program a computer controlled opponent :). They keys are:Left Player[A] Go Left[D] Go Right[W] Go Up[S] Go Down[Cntl] Shoot/Release Ball[Shift] Point the other wayRight Player[Left Arrow] Go Left[Right Arrow] Go Right[Up Arrow] Go Up[Down Arrow] Go Down[Space] Shoot/Release Ball[Cmnd] Point the other wayWhat else... oh, every time someone scores, their score marker will go up. There is no limit on the game, so you decide when to finish, by clicking the mouse.About the graphics and sounds, the graphics for the ships were blatantly stolen from Escape Velocity. I could go on and make my own ships, but I would need to learn some 3D package. The same goes for the few sounds there are in the game, they have been stolen from other games I had lying around in my HD (some of them are from the Simpsons :). If anyone has a nice 3D modeled ship that could work for this, I would happily use it. Also, I could use a better background. I know it sucks, but until 2 days ago, the background was a picture of Metallica's James Hetfield holding his black ESP Explorer guitar, so don't complain ;).If you were wondering, the mini-explosions that appear when the bullets hit something are also stolen from EV. Sosume.Well thats it, I hope it amuses you. I would appreciate if you could send me any comments or suggestions on how to improve the game if you think it's worth improving.As you probably noticed, there is no interface at all in the game. It is actually already programmed, it's just deactivated because I found it too much of a hassle to go File>New Game everytime I wanted to play. If I ever add any features requiring it, I will activate it and add a nice splash screen.¨2002 Eduardo Ojeda. Made using Sprite Animation Toolkit by Ingemar Rangnemalm.